fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7127517Z   ok   a tank's terminal credit survives intact when the house is drawing hard
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7127733Z   ok   and collapses to nothing when the house needs no bought heat at all
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7127952Z   ok   with no cliff between the two: the discount is continuous in demand
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7128149Z   ok   a better-insulated tank is discounted less than a bare one
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7128364Z   ok   a tank that loses nothing keeps its whole credit, even with no demand
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7128593Z   ok   the discount does not depend on the end temperature the solver picks
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7128785Z   ok   free gains that cover the whole loss leave no hold demand
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7128955Z   ok   and solar is only counted when the caller asks for it
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7129172Z   ok   so in summer the tank's terminal credit is switched off entirely
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7129371Z   ok   while at -5 C the same tank keeps essentially all of it
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7129572Z   ok   and without a valve the discount is exactly 1.0, changing nothing
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7129743Z   ok   without a valve the terminal cost ignores the tank
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7129888Z   ok   a 35 L tank behind a valve is not a store
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7130027Z   ok   so its settlement cap stays the slab's
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7130159Z   ok   and the terminal cost ignores it
