fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7162744Z -- Two-tank topology (issue #40)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7162911Z   ok   without a valve the layout is the valveless one
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163117Z   ok   a valve, two zones and a wood probe resolve to the 4-way layout
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163271Z   ok   a valve without a wood probe stays single-tank
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163454Z   ok   a flue switch alone does not activate the two-tank model
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163624Z   ok   and neither does a wood probe without a second zone
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163758Z   ok   one number sizes the one physical tank
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7163952Z   ok   a gated-on model with no wood reading reduces byte-for-byte
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7164095Z   ok   and reports no wood trajectory at all
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7164323Z   ok   the wood tank is drawn while it can meet the curve, hotter tank or not
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7164516Z   ok   the blend fraction is the one the outlet estimator measures
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7164744Z   ok   below the curve both tanks fall back to a smooth hotter-source switch
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7164952Z   ok   sweeping the curve across both boundaries moves the draw smoothly
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7165200Z   ok   and so does sweeping the wood tank up through the curve
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7165438Z   ok   wood_share is continuous as wood_temp crosses the flow curve in region 3
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7165656Z   ok   wood_share is continuous as hp_temp crosses the flow curve in region 3
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7165844Z   ok   the batched twin carries the same hp-boundary continuity
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7166074Z   ok   the vector wood_share path stays bitwise-identical to the scalar law
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7166213Z   ok   a burn charges the wood tank, pointwise
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7166388Z   ok   and takes no cap headroom from the heat pump's tank
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7166600Z   ok   the burn moves load off the heat pump's tank rather than into it
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7166806Z   ok   which is exactly what the single-tank abstraction could not do
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167000Z   ok   so wood heat no longer shows up as a heat pump COP penalty
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167184Z   ok   the emitters got what the valve outlet says they got
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167334Z   ok   and one two-tank step balances to the last bit
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167560Z   ok   a ceiling-saturating burn leaves the whole-system identity closed
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167728Z   ok   the 95 C ceiling's refusal is booked, not deleted
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7167928Z   ok   a tank the burn cannot saturate books nothing and still balances
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7168129Z   ok   a wood tank read above the ceiling cools at its physical rate
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7168352Z   ok   the tank's rate divides by the capacity the tank has, not by the guard
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7168643Z   ok   and is unchanged above the guard (10 L floor, 200 L null arm)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7168818Z   ok   the wood tank's rate divides by its own capacity too
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7169051Z   ok   the refill coil takes the same heat from a 5 L wood tank as a 200 L one
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7169267Z   ok   the batched two-zone step divides by the same capacity, bit for bit
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7169476Z   ok   and its schedule is one the compared axes can see the divisor in
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7169666Z   ok   a DHW tank below the guard still takes the heat it is given
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7169870Z   ok   the tank's own standby coast time does not depend on what it holds
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7170107Z   ok   a weather array left at its default is the zero array, on every simulator
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7170283Z   ok   and each of those arrays is live at these parameters
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7170490Z   ok   six hours of two-tank operation does not depend on the step length
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7170680Z   ok   a 10 L wood tank cannot discharge below what it is feeding
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7170864Z   ok   and it empties into the house rather than through zero
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7171061Z   ok   a cold wood tank and no burn is byte-identical to no wood tank
