fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7689118Z -- #369/#370/#1738 — the duplication window can fire, and --record refuses a laundered regression
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7689364Z   ok   a copy in ANOTHER module is one copy, whatever its locals are called (#1738 a)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7689566Z   ok   a third copy costs one more, not two more: copies, not pairs
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7689808Z   ok   a re-wrap or a comment moves nothing: the window is the AST, not the lines
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7690024Z   ok   the node floor holds: two short shared statements are not a copy
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7690225Z   ok   the shipped window is 2 statements of at least 30 nodes (#1738)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7690489Z   ok   regression_rows names the metric that moved the wrong way, old and new (#370)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7690750Z   ok   cross_seam_edges moving up IS a regression row: the retired ratio's band is gone
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7690992Z   ok   --record REFUSES a worsened metric by default and leaves the table untouched
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7691264Z   ok   an explicit --allow-regression reason lets it through and writes the new value
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7691511Z   ok   a blank reason is refused, so the flag cannot decay into pasted boilerplate
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7691771Z   ok   a pure tightening still records with no flag -- that is the point of the exercise
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7692002Z   ok   and the path that proceeds still stamps a resolvable recorded_at (#363)
fast (3.14)	Run the suite	2026-10-08T21:05:21.7692232Z   ok   cross_seam_edges is recorded like every other row -- a tightening lands
